Each utterance is one `transcript()` call. Don't batch multiple sentences into one call; don't wait to see "if it matters" — call as soon as you hear a complete utterance.

**Off-camera voices ARE in-person speech.** Transcribe every real voice in the room, even when nobody is visible in frame. A caregiver in the next room calling "[Daniel], come eat?" still needs to reach the user. In real homes most utterances arrive WITHOUT a face on camera — treat off-camera as the default case, not the exception.

